.9%  (backwards)\n- the combined score: best fifth -0.3%, worst fifth +0.4%  (backwards)\n\nEACH WAY OF SCORING, top 20 a month (older half / newer half; all stocks -0.7% / +0.2%; S&P 500 +0.8% / +1.3%)\n- all four measures: -0.6% / -0.6%\n- strength over 6 months only: -1.0% / +1.8%\n- closeness to the high only: -0.6% / -0.4%\n- calm moves only: -1.5% / -1.1%\n- a recent dip only: -1.3% / -2.0%\n\nVERDICT: REJECTED. The top-scored stocks did worse than the average stock in the newer half. Do not buy by this score.\n\nNo top-scored list: the score is rejected, so its picks are not shown (they would only mislead).\n\nPaper baskets: the first one is recorded today and judged in a month.\nAbout 4 years of monthly tests (plus 6 months to warm up), one market climate; price measures only (no company figures in this history). Research, not an order. Not financial advice, not a halal ruling."}